### Describe the bug

In crates/precompiles/src/stablecoin_exchange/mod.rs, orders with the same tick are arranged in a linked list, corresponding to one level. In the `process_pending_order function`, when a level is newly created, its tick is checked and the best_tick may be updated.

```
let prev_tail = level.tail;
if prev_tail == 0 {
    level.head = order_id;
    level.tail = order_id;

    Orderbook::set_tick_bit(self, order.book_key(), order.tick(), order.is_bid())
        .expect("Tick is valid");

    if order.is_bid() {
        if order.tick() > orderbook.best_bid_tick {
            Orderbook::update_best_bid_tick(self, order.book_key(), order.tick())?; // ===> update best tick
        }
    } else if order.tick() < orderbook.best_ask_tick {
        Orderbook::update_best_ask_tick(self, order.book_key(), order.tick())?; // ===> update best tick
    }
}
```

In subsequent transactions, the contract matches orders from the best_tick queue.However, in both the `fill_order` and `cancel_active_order` functions, the orders at a certain tick may be exhausted, but neither place checks whether the best_tick should be updated at this time:

```
let next_tick_info = if order.next() == 0 {
    Orderbook::delete_tick_level(self, book_key, order.is_bid(), order.tick())?;

    Orderbook::clear_tick_bit(self, order.book_key(), order.tick(), order.is_bid())
        .expect("Tick is valid");

    let (tick, has_liquidity) =
        Orderbook::next_initialized_tick(self, book_key, order.is_bid(), order.tick());
    // ===> just delete, clear and search next
}
......
// If this was the last order at this tick, clear the bitmap bit
if level.head == 0 {
    Orderbook::clear_tick_bit(self, order.book_key(), order.tick(), order.is_bid()) // ===> just clear bit_map
        .expect("Tick is valid");
}
```

Then, `get_best_price_level` may return an incorrect level. Since the level.head is 0 at this time, the 0th order is used first in subsequent transactions, which may lead to:
1. Transactions deviate from the expected processing logic, starting from order 0 instead of the best order;
2. The tick 0 queue may be mistakenly deleted and the corresponding bitmap cleared, so the orders in this queue will never be selected for trading and can only be canceled;
